## Architecture (v2 — Hardened)

The Carsales ingestion follows a two-tier architecture with strict safety controls:

**Global Kill Switch:** `CRAWL_MODE=disabled` env secret instantly stops ALL Carsales crawling. No Apify calls, no queuing, no retries. Clean 200 response.

**Tier 1 — Shallow Sweep (every 2h):** `carsales-scan-cron` scans all 8 AU states SERIALISED (one at a time, 10s gaps). 200 items per state. No retries on failure.

**Tier 2 — Deep Market Pricing (daily):** `carsales-deep-scan-cron` scrapes 25 make/model buckets SERIALISED (12s gaps). 150 items per bucket. Auto-halts after 3 consecutive lock-skips (backpressure protection).

**Concurrency Lock:** `carsales-scan` checks `apify_runs_queue` for any active carsales run (status=queued|running). If one exists, the launch is skipped. This prevents ALL parallel Carsales runs.

**URL Validation:** Every URL must be a fully filtered `carsales.com.au/cars/` search URL with `q=` filter params. Bare pages, missing filters, or malformed URLs are rejected before any Apify call.

**Apify Defaults:** timeout=20000s, memory=1024MB, maxItems capped at 250.

**Structured Responses:** All paths return `{ok, status, ...}` objects: `skipped_disabled`, `skipped_invalid_url`, `skipped_already_running`, `launched`, `launch_failed`, `config_missing`.

**No Retries:** Failed runs log and stop. Next scheduled cycle or manual intervention required. No cost bleed from retry loops.

**Env Vars That Matter:**
- `CRAWL_MODE` — set to "disabled" to kill all Carsales crawling
- `APIFY_TOKEN` — Apify API token
- `APIFY_ACTOR_ID_CARSALES` — actor identifier (slash or tilde format)
